libisal
------------------------------------------
ISA-L is a collection of optimized low-level functions targeting storage
applications.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libisal-devel-2.32.1-1bl1
  libisal2-2.32.1-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.8-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.4-1
  cygport-0.37.10-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  help2man-1.49.3-1
  nasm-2.16.03-2
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/intel/isa-l

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/intel/isa-l/archive/refs/tags/v2.32.1.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack libisal-2.32.1-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./libisal-2.32.1-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/libisal-2.32.1-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libisal-2.32.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libisal2-2.32.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libisal-devel-2.32.1-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

